---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Cascadia Mobile Research">
  <!-- Hero Section -->
  <section class="hero-topo section bg-gradient-to-b from-dark-bg via-dark-surface to-dark-bg">
    <div class="container-custom">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl">
        <h1 class="mb-8 text-center text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-5xl lg:text-6xl">
          From Field to <span class="text-gradient">Map</span>
        </h1>
        <div class="mb-8 border-l-4 border-accent-blue bg-dark-surface/50 p-6 text-lg leading-relaxed">
          <p class="text-text-primary">
            <strong>Cascadia Mobile Research is a Portland, Oregon lab that collects field data with
            drones and LiDAR, processes it on infrastructure we own and operate, and delivers it as
            maps, 3D models, and measurements.</strong>
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl space-y-4 text-center text-lg text-text-secondary">
          <p>
            We are a small, independent outfit: real instruments, our own compute, and an open lab
            notebook. Every capability we advertise is one we can demonstrate.
          </p>
          <p>
            Client work funds the lab. The lab publishes its methods. Each makes the other better.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="mt-10 flex flex-col items-center justify-center gap-4 sm:flex-row">
          <a href="/services" class="btn btn-primary">
            View Services
          </a>
          <a href="/research" class="btn btn-secondary">
            Read the Lab Notes
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Pipeline -->
  <section class="section border-t border-dark-border">
    <div class="container-custom">
      <h2 class="mb-12 text-center text-3xl font-bold sm:text-4xl">One Pipeline, End to End</h2>
      <div class="grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-3">
        <div class="card">
          <svg class="mb-4 h-8 w-8 text-accent-blue" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" aria-hidden="true">
            <circle cx="5" cy="5" r="2.4"/><circle cx="19" cy="5" r="2.4"/><circle cx="5" cy="19" r="2.4"/><circle cx="19" cy="19" r="2.4"/>
            <path stroke-linecap="round" d="M6.8 6.8l3 3m7.4-3l-3 3m-4.4 4.4l-3 3m10.4-3l3 3"/>
            <rect x="9.8" y="9.8" width="4.4" height="4.4" rx="1.2"/>
          </svg>
          <h3 class="mb-3 text-lg font-semibold text-accent-blue">1 · Collect</h3>
          <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
            Field data capture with a lightweight sub-250g drone platform and a handheld 3D LiDAR
            scanner. Planned, repeatable flights and scans — the same site can be captured the same
            way next month, so change over time is measurable.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
          <svg class="mb-4 h-8 w-8 text-accent-cyan" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" aria-hidden="true">
            <rect x="6.5" y="6.5" width="11" height="11" rx="2"/>
            <rect x="10" y="10" width="4" height="4" rx="1"/>
            <path stroke-linecap="round" d="M9 6.5V3.5m6 3V3.5M9 20.5v-3m6 3v-3M6.5 9h-3m3 6h-3M20.5 9h-3m3 6h-3"/>
          </svg>
          <h3 class="mb-3 text-lg font-semibold text-accent-cyan">2 · Process</h3>
          <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
            Photogrammetry, LiDAR SLAM, and analysis run on our own GPU workstation and
            virtualization cluster. Your imagery and scan data are processed in-house — they never
            pass through a third-party cloud service.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
          <svg class="mb-4 h-8 w-8 text-accent-green" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" aria-hidden="true">
            <path stroke-linejoin="round" d="M9 4.5L3.5 6.5v13L9 17.5l6 2 5.5-2v-13l-5.5 2-6-2z"/>
            <path stroke-linecap="round" d="M9 4.5v13m6-11v13"/>
            <path stroke-linecap="round" d="M5.5 12.5c1.5-1 2.5.5 4-.5s2-2 3.5-1.5"/>
          </svg>
          <h3 class="mb-3 text-lg font-semibold text-accent-green">3 · Deliver</h3>
          <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
            Orthomosaics, elevation models, point clouds, textured 3D meshes, and GIS analysis —
            delivered in standard formats with notes on how they were produced and what their
            accuracy limits are.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- What We Do -->
  <section class="section bg-dark-surface">
    <div class="container-custom">
      <h2 class="mb-12 text-center text-3xl font-bold sm:text-4xl">What We Do</h2>
      <div class="grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4">
        <div class="card card-hover">
          <h3 class="mb-3 text-lg font-semibold text-accent-blue">
            Aerial Mapping &amp; Photogrammetry
          </h3>
          <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
            Drone-captured imagery reconstructed into orthomosaics, elevation models, and 3D site
            models.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="card card-hover">
          <h3 class="mb-3 text-lg font-semibold text-accent-cyan">
            LiDAR Scanning &amp; 3D Modeling
          </h3>
          <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
            Ground-based LiDAR capture of structures, sites, and interiors, processed into point
            clouds and meshes.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="card card-hover">
          <h3 class="mb-3 text-lg font-semibold text-accent-green">
            Inspection &amp; Monitoring
          </h3>
          <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
            Aerial documentation of roofs, structures, and construction progress with repeatable
            capture plans.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="card card-hover">
          <h3 class="mb-3 text-lg font-semibold text-accent-purple">
            GIS &amp; Spatial Analysis
          </h3>
          <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
            Cartography, spatial analysis, and change detection that turn captured data into
            answers.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="mt-10 text-center">
        <a href="/services" class="btn btn-secondary">Full service details</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Why Self-Hosted -->
  <section class="section border-t border-dark-border">
    <div class="container-custom">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl">
        <h2 class="mb-12 text-center text-3xl font-bold sm:text-4xl">Why We Run Our Own Infrastructure</h2>
        <div class="grid items-center gap-10 lg:grid-cols-2">
          <div class="space-y-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
            <p>
              Most drone service providers upload client data to third-party cloud platforms for
              processing. We don't. Every pipeline we use — photogrammetry, LiDAR SLAM, machine
              learning — runs on hardware we own, in a stack we can inspect end to end.
            </p>
            <p>
              That matters for clients who can't ship data to someone else's cloud: public agencies,
              infrastructure operators, and anyone with data-governance requirements. It also matters
              for quality — when we control the whole pipeline, we can measure it, tune it, and
              explain exactly how a deliverable was produced.
            </p>
            <p>
              The infrastructure is also a research subject in its own right. We benchmark and
              document our processing stack publicly in the <a href="/research" class="link">lab
              notes</a>.
            </p>
          </div>
          <figure>
            <div class="img-frame">
              <img
                src="/images/terrain-flightplan.webp"
                alt="Dark shaded-relief terrain map with cyan contour lines and a green lawnmower-pattern drone survey flight plan over a marked survey area"
                width="1400"
                height="788"
                loading="lazy"
                class="w-full"
              />
            </div>
            <figcaption class="img-caption">
              Survey flight planning over terrain — synthetic data, rendered in-lab on our own stack.
            </figcaption>
          </figure>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Lab Notes Teaser -->
  <section class="section bg-dark-surface">
    <div class="container-custom">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl">
        <h2 class="mb-12 text-center text-3xl font-bold sm:text-4xl">An Open Lab Notebook</h2>
        <div class="grid items-center gap-10 lg:grid-cols-2">
          <figure class="order-last lg:order-first">
            <div class="img-frame">
              <img
                src="/images/pointcloud-scan.webp"
                alt="LiDAR-style 3D point cloud of terrain with a scanned gabled structure, points colored blue to cyan by elevation on a dark background"
                width="1280"
                height="740"
                loading="lazy"
                class="w-full"
              />
            </div>
            <figcaption class="img-caption">
              Point cloud of a structure on terrain — synthetic scan, visualized with our processing
              pipeline.
            </figcaption>
          </figure>
          <div>
            <div class="space-y-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
              <p>
                We publish our experiments, benchmarks, and field methodology as we go — including
                negative results. Current questions on the bench: how does low-cost drone
                photogrammetry compare to LiDAR SLAM for site reconstruction accuracy? What does
                self-hosted photogrammetry actually cost against cloud services? What does a
                survey-grade corridor mapping deliverable look like from a sub-250g platform?
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="mt-8">
              <a href="/research" class="btn btn-primary">Lab Notes</a>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Current Status -->
  <section class="section border-t border-dark-border">
    <div class="container-custom">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl text-center">
        <h2 class="mb-6 text-3xl font-bold sm:text-4xl">Current Status</h2>
        <div class="mb-8 inline-flex items-center rounded-full border border-accent-green/30 bg-accent-green/10 px-4 py-2">
          <span class="mr-2 h-2 w-2 rounded-full bg-accent-green"></span>
          <span class="text-sm font-medium text-accent-green">Early Operations</span>
        </div>
        <p class="mb-8 text-text-secondary">
          Cascadia Mobile Research LLC is an Oregon limited liability company in its first year of
          operations. The instrument kit, processing pipeline, and lab notebook are all under active
          development — expect this site to grow as work is published.
        </p>
        <div class="flex flex-col items-center justify-center gap-4 sm:flex-row">
          <a href="/about" class="btn btn-primary">
            About the Lab
          </a>
          <a
            href="https://github.com/cascadia-systems-lab"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="btn btn-secondary"
          >
            View on GitHub
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
